ENTRY            23365   20260331   20260827   20260827       2324
SUBENT        23365001   20260331   20260827   20260827       2324
BIB                 12         89
TITLE      Cross section and neutron angular distribution
            measurements of neutron scattering on natural iron
AUTHOR     (E.Pirovano, R.Beyer, M.Dietz, A.R.Junghans,
            S.E.Muller, R.Nolte, M.Nyman, A.J.M.Plompen, M.Roder,
            T.Szucs, M.P.Takacs)
INSTITUTE  (2ZZZGEL,2GERZFK,2GERDRE,2GERPTB)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,99,024601,2019)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.99.024601
           (R,INDC(BLG)-2,2017)
           (J,EPJ/CS,146,11008,2017)
           #doi:10.1051/epjconf/201714611008
            Fe(n,n0) DA and SIG in figs
           (R,INDC(EUR)-0042,2026)
           #doi:10.61092/iaea.3e74-pjcw
            Details on Legendre coefficient determination
INC-SOURCE (PHOTO)
            GELINA:
             Nominal average beam energy:  100 MeV
             Nominal average peak current:  70 uA
             Repetition rate:              800 Hz
             Pulse width:          typically 1 ns (FWHM)
             Primary neutron production target:
                U-Mo alloy with 10wt% of Mo, depleted uranium
             Moderator:
                Unmoderated flux configuration
             Flight path direction:
                108 deg from the electron beam direction
             Neutron beam diameter at sample: 4.9(2) cm
            nELBE:
             Nominal average beam energy:   30 MeV
             Nominal average peak current:  15 uA
             Repetition rate:              101 kHz
             Pulse width (typical):          5 ps
             Primary neutron production target:
                Liquid Pb loop
             Moderator:
                No moderator
             Flight path direction:
                95 deg from the electron beam direction
             Neutron beam diameter at sample: 7.40(1) cm
METHOD     (TOF)
            GELINA:
             Source-scattering distance:      27.037(5) m
             Source-fission chamber distance: 25.667(5) m
             TOF resolution:                          5 ns
             Energy resolution (at 1 MeV):            5 keV
            nELBE:
             Source-scattering distance:       8.300(5) m
             Source-fission chamber distance:  6.044(5) m
             TOF resolution:                          1 ns
             Energy resolution (at 1 MeV):            3 keV
DETECTOR   (SCIN) EJ301 and EJ315 liquid organic scintillators,
            (cylindrical, 5.08 cm diam.x5.08 cm high, 105.9 cm3),
             which front face is placed at a distance of
             0.300(3) m from the center of the sample.
            Four detectors (two in horizontal, two at 60 deg with
             the horizontal plane facing downward) at each of the
             following angles (deg):
              163.8(1), 142.8(1), 121.7(1), 100.6(1), 79.4(1),
              58.3(1), 37.2(1), 16.2(1).
            The scintillator absolute neutron response was
             determined in a TOF experiment using carbon (neutron
             elastic scattering cross section standard) as
             scattering sample.
           (FISCH) UF4 deposited on Al (8 deposits of 70 mm diam.,
            4.095(4) mg/cm2)
CORRECTION - Dead time
           - Background subtraction
             . Photon-induced events discriminated via pulse
               shape analysis
             . Neutron background - room return neutron
               determination and sample-in/sample-out
               measurements
           - Multiple scattering
               Correction factor determined via Monte Carlo
               simulations.
           - Elastic/inelastic reaction separation
               via neutron spectrometry (deconvolution of the
               detector response).
MONITOR    (92-U-235(N,F),,SIG)
MONIT-REF  (,,3,ENDF/B-VII.1,,2011)
STATUS     (TABLE) Data received from Elisa Pirovano
           (APRVD) Proof-read by Elisa Pirovano (2017-12-01)
HISTORY    (20171128R) On
           (20171130C) On
           (20190228A) VS Ref. Phys.Rev.C99(2019)024601 added.
            Partial angular distributions for scattering from the
            first excited level of 56Fe compiled in 008-009.
           (20260331A) On. 010, 011 and 012 added.
ENDBIB              89
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           92
SUBENT        23365002   20171130   20180903   20180809       2266
BIB                  4         12
REACTION   (6-C-0(N,EL)6-C-0,,DA)
FACILITY   (LINAC,2ZZZGEL) GELINA
SAMPLE      Natural graphite disk
             Thickness:     0.0832(2) at/b
             Sample mass:  130.424(5) g
             Surface dimension: 10.00(1) cm diam.x0.99(1) cm thick
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) Propagated from uncertainties due to
            - statistics,
            - Monte-Carlo model for the detector response
               modelling,
            - beam monitoring with the fission (common for all
               detectors)
ENDBIB              12
